# nvn: (1) the MTLDevice pipeline archive (0414) leaves out pipelines without a fragment stage on iOS; (2) DM_NVN_RENDER_COND=0
# ignores render conditions
#
# Why: South Park: The Fractured But Whole (01008F2005154000), iPhone 15 Pro, iOS 27.2.1, 2026-11-22.
#   (1) "[RED] pipeline binary archive: the write failed (Failed to generate machO ... expecting 'fragment' stage in pipeline no. '10')", then "off for this run". A vertex-only
#       render pipeline (rasterization disabled) added to the archive made every later write fail.
#   (2) Stretches of frames encoded no draw (draft 0508 counts why). The prime suspect is a render condition the host evaluates false on the CPU, and that needs a switch to try
#       from the game's env.txt without a rebuild.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m; two tests):
#   (1) dva_storable, at dva_offer and again at dva_add (an entry queued before): a render or mesh pipeline with no fragment function, no vertex function, or rasterization
#       disabled is built as before but left out of the archive.
#       Counted, logged once ("pipeline archive: pipelines without a fragment stage are left out ..."), and the count is in every "written" line
#       ("pipeline archive: N pipelines without a fragment stage left out").
#       Default on iOS only. A Mac writes such pipelines and finds them again, and 0414's t_pso_binary_archive relies on that. DM_PSO_ARCHIVE_NOFRAG=1 leaves them out
#       anywhere, 0 keeps them anywhere.
#       No persistent poison, unchanged from 0414: the off state is per process, and the file on disk is the last good write. DVA_FAIL_SESSIONS runs in a row that end on a
#       failed write start the file again empty. With the filter, the pipeline that caused it is no longer offered, so the next session writes normally.
#   (2) DM_NVN_RENDER_COND=0: SetRenderEnableConditional blocks are still evaluated and counted (0508's true / false / unknown) but never drop anything: draws and clears run, as
#       before the host evaluated conditions. Logged once when set.
#       The draws a false condition would have dropped are counted ("render condition ignored ..." at 1-4 and powers of two; the total in 0508's 300-present line).
#       SetRenderEnable(false), the game's own switch, is kept. Default 1: evaluated, as now.
#       0508's per-reason counts still count. render_condition_false then stays 0 for conditional blocks; the would-be drops are g_rc_ignored.
# Env names (games/<id>/env.txt, read by the app's apply_env_files: DM_* names; no launcher row needed): DM_NVN_RENDER_COND=0, DM_PSO_ARCHIVE_NOFRAG=0|1.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Tests (M1 Pro, tree = base + 0506 + 0507 + 0508 + 0509):
#   - t_pso_archive_nofrag (new, make check_t_pso_archive_nofrag) 11/0;
#   - t_render_cond_switch (new, make check_t_render_cond_switch: default and DM_NVN_RENDER_COND=0) 4/0 + 5/0;
#   - 0414's check_t_pso_binary_archive 22 sessions / 0 failed;
#   - t_nvn 506/0, t_dead_targets 197/0, t_drop_reasons 13/0, t_present_keep 10/0, t_vbuf_clamp 15/0.
#   NOT run on a device; no host dylib built. The iPhone's write failure itself was not reproduced on the Mac (macOS writes such pipelines fine).

# Rebased 2026-11-22 onto the new 0506 (upstream c96c45e9 + 79555b67 + the pool-end fallback): context only, same behaviour.

